From fa70bd110eda5569af7e4e4c79fdd5e9aa0076d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stanley <stanley.chang@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:21:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 110/122] script: acpi: mc-setup.sh: add ZED X (MAX9295D
 multi-PHY) support

Teach the generic maxim-serdes media-controller setup script to handle a
ZED X: two AR0234 sensors behind one MAX9295D (INTC1140) serializer.

- Discover cameras per PHY (DESn.CHmm.SERk.CHpp.CAMp); key camera state
  by (des, link, phy) and take the serializer sink pad from the live
  media graph.
- Probe the ar0234 source stream (driver uses stream 1 for the 0x18
  sensor) instead of assuming STREAM_NODE.
- Accumulate serializer routes per serializer so both PHYs are programmed
  in a single -R; MAX9295D source stream follows the sink pad / pipe.
- Give ZED X sensors a fixed per-DES slot (ACPI path order) used as both
  CSI2 capture pad and deserializer source stream / VC, matching the
  camera HAL ar0234stereo.json; other cameras take the remaining streams.
- New CLI token phy=P to select one sensor of a multi-PHY link.
- When a ZED X is configured: set ar0234 frame_sync (ZEDX_FRAME_SYNC,
  default 1), prepare PSYS and create /dev/video-ar0234-* links.

D457/ISX031 routing and formats are unchanged.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
